Backport two Dovecot fixes into the Alpine 3.24 package used by the IMAP and
front images. IMAP now keeps the TLS socket open through the post-login handoff,
enables Dovecot's Thunderbird client workarounds, and sends empty partial FETCH
results in a form accepted by affected iOS Mail clients. The front and storage
Dovecot services no longer advertise IMAP DEFLATE compression, which avoids the
compression-related disconnect seen with Apple Mail.
